1
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:40,465
- What have you got for me?
- Nothing. You killed Roger of Stoke.

2
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,474
Allan...

3
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:45,978
You knew I'd kill him.
You just couldn't admit it to yourself.

4
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:47,979
- You're low.
- Yeah.

5
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:52,007
And you are here for more money,
so what do you want to tell me?

6
00:00:52,085 --> 00:00:57,352
You've got a messenger, Henry of Lewes,
arriving tomorrow, right?

7
00:00:58,992 --> 00:01:00,289
How do you know that?

8
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:04,694
He's coming to tell you where and when
the King plans to land on his return.

9
00:01:04,764 --> 00:01:08,029
There's going to be an ambush tomorrow
on the north road

10
00:01:08,101 --> 00:01:10,626
so you'd better change his route.

11
00:01:13,973 --> 00:01:15,338
'Ey - what do you call this?

12
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,205
Noon tomorrow.

13
00:01:17,277 --> 00:01:18,869
Gold.

14
00:01:21,114 --> 00:01:23,446
If Henry arrives.

15
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:40,198
He's not coming.

16
00:01:41,401 --> 00:01:44,029
- He's been tipped off.
- By who?

17
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:46,538
Don't worry, he's just late.

18
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:50,235
Horse needs shoeing or he's stopped
for a kip or something.

19
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:53,438
He's betraying the King.
He's not going to stop for a nap.

20
00:01:53,513 --> 00:01:56,004
Could Marian have got the time wrong?

21
00:01:56,082 --> 00:02:00,178
That's a good point, actually.
Cos she's listening through keyholes.

22
00:02:01,421 --> 00:02:04,151
She could be making all kinds of mistakes.

23
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,557
She could be making a big mistake.

24
00:02:11,364 --> 00:02:14,629
Go back to the camp and stay there.

25
00:02:15,435 --> 00:02:17,733
- Robin
- But...

26
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:19,795
That's an order.

27
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,137
Robin!

28
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:28,812
- My lord!
- What do you think?

29
00:02:28,882 --> 00:02:31,976
Hastings or Portsmouth?

30
00:02:32,051 --> 00:02:37,148
Which south coast port will King Richard
make his final, fateful landing at, mm?

31
00:02:37,223 --> 00:02:40,920
We'll know soon enough. Henry's here.

32
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:43,724
- As I promised.
- Well done, Gisborne.

33
00:02:43,796 --> 00:02:45,195
Well done.

34
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:49,462
Now, Henry...

35
00:02:52,972 --> 00:02:55,236
Henry of Lewes!

36
00:02:57,243 --> 00:03:01,612
Welcome to my...

37
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:06,783
Get me my physician.

38
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:09,321
Get the Sheriff's physician, immediately.

39
00:03:11,057 --> 00:03:14,220
- Why did you let the messenger through?
- Has he talked?

40
00:03:14,294 --> 00:03:16,558
No, not yet. He was taken ill.

41
00:03:16,629 --> 00:03:20,622
Robin, I took a risk to find out his route
and you still let him through.

42
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,567
- You can't go back into the castle.
- What?

43
00:03:23,636 --> 00:03:26,036
Go to the forest, now.

44
00:03:26,105 --> 00:03:28,403
I'll join you when I've silenced Henry.

45
00:03:28,474 --> 00:03:31,238
The forest? Don't be ridiculous.

46
00:03:31,311 --> 00:03:34,144
- You told me he'd travel by the north road.
- Yes.

47
00:03:34,214 --> 00:03:35,579
And he didn't.

48
00:03:37,350 --> 00:03:41,252
Marian, I think I have a spy in my gang.

49
00:04:24,230 --> 00:04:26,391
What are you going to do?

50
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:35,005
I'll silence Henry...

51
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:39,002
and then I'll find the traitor
in my own camp

52
00:04:39,078 --> 00:04:40,773
and silence him.

53
00:04:40,847 --> 00:04:44,248
None of your men have been in the castle.
I would've seen them.

54
00:04:44,350 --> 00:04:47,581
- So somebody's going out to meet them.
- I'll keep watch.

55
00:04:47,654 --> 00:04:49,519
No. You'll keep out of it.

56
00:04:49,589 --> 00:04:51,989
- No!
- This is none of your business.

57
00:04:52,058 --> 00:04:55,994
The King is being betrayed
because of your spy, it is my business.

58
00:04:56,062 --> 00:04:58,223
He might know
about the Nightwatchman.

59
00:04:58,298 --> 00:04:59,822
Then I'm dead anyway.

60
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:14,241
- What are you doing? He's worse.
- He's calmer.

61
00:05:14,347 --> 00:05:16,042
Calmer?

62
00:05:16,849 --> 00:05:21,445
- You're calming him to death.
- Medicine is a journey, not a destination.

63
00:05:21,554 --> 00:05:23,317
Treatments take as long as...

64
00:05:23,389 --> 00:05:26,984
Do you think I've got time
for your journey, Blight? A clue.

65
00:05:28,261 --> 00:05:32,823
Gisborne, you find me a quack
who knows what he's doing.

66
00:05:32,899 --> 00:05:34,332
- My lord.
- A quack?

67
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:37,733
Sheriff, I am a man of learning,
I give you science.

68
00:05:37,804 --> 00:05:40,034
Science? You have given me silence.

69
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:43,642
I want this man to talk.

70
00:05:56,823 --> 00:06:00,224
- What are you doing here?
- What are you doing here?

71
00:06:01,694 --> 00:06:06,131
I know you're angry that Henry of Lewes
got past us but you can't just run off.

72
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:11,600
Much, you disobeyed my instructions.
I said wait at the camp.

73
00:06:11,671 --> 00:06:13,730
Gisborne has outwitted us.

74
00:06:13,806 --> 00:06:17,207
So what? His luck'll run out, it has to.

75
00:06:18,311 --> 00:06:21,974
Otherwise we'll be asking where
he's getting his information from.

76
00:06:24,751 --> 00:06:26,946
What?

77
00:06:29,622 --> 00:06:32,113
You think he's getting information?

78
00:06:33,559 --> 00:06:35,959
From one of us?

79
00:06:36,028 --> 00:06:39,361
No. Master, surely some mistake.

80
00:06:39,432 --> 00:06:41,229
A traitor?

81
00:06:43,269 --> 00:06:45,396
Who?

82
00:06:45,471 --> 00:06:47,632
That's why you sent us back to camp,

83
00:06:47,707 --> 00:06:49,766
because you suspect.

84
00:06:51,177 --> 00:06:54,578
- You suspect me?
- I have to suspect everyone.

85
00:06:54,647 --> 00:06:57,616
- That's me. You suspect me.
- Much, go back to the camp.

86
00:06:57,683 --> 00:07:00,948
What do I have to do to prove my loyalty?
What? Tell me!

87
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:02,749
What?

88
00:07:02,822 --> 00:07:05,052
I'll chop off my own arms.

89
00:07:05,158 --> 00:07:09,595
Well, one arm, cos once I'd chopped that
off, I couldn't chop off the other...

90
00:07:12,231 --> 00:07:15,029
If you're true to me,
I ask just one thing.

91
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:17,535
- You name it.
- Go back to the camp.

92
00:07:24,377 --> 00:07:25,605
Ooh!

93
00:07:29,048 --> 00:07:30,811
Come, come, come.

94
00:07:32,351 --> 00:07:34,251
There you go.

95
00:07:35,855 --> 00:07:39,086
Oh! This baby's just like his mother.

96
00:07:39,158 --> 00:07:41,752
- Doesn't know up from down.
- Oh, again?

97
00:07:41,828 --> 00:07:44,854
Oh, again! Don't you bother yourself.

98
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:46,591
I'll turn him the right way up.

99
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:50,329
- How do you know it's a boy?
- Because I know.

100
00:07:52,271 --> 00:07:54,739
- Hup!
- But it hurts.

101
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:57,401
Hurts?! You don't know pain.

102
00:07:57,477 --> 00:08:01,038
Try giving birth to him feet first.
Then you'll know what pain is.

103
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:06,216
Bring her medicines.
The Sheriff wants your services.

104
00:08:06,285 --> 00:08:09,914
- Get off me! My daughter!
- Your daughter can wait.

105
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:11,957
Mother!

106
00:08:13,192 --> 00:08:16,355
- Mother!
- You hairy, pig-witted fox turd.

107
00:08:16,429 --> 00:08:20,957
I'll pluck your eyeballs from your bony
skull and squelch them into cesspits.

108
00:08:21,033 --> 00:08:23,467
- Mother!
- Rosa!

109
00:08:23,569 --> 00:08:25,867
Speak!

110
00:08:25,972 --> 00:08:27,564
Speak, speak.

111
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:30,336
Speak!

112
00:08:30,409 --> 00:08:32,343
- Get off me.
- Silent, woman.

113
00:08:32,411 --> 00:08:35,505
You slimy little snot-head.

114
00:08:36,549 --> 00:08:38,915
- Matilda!
- Blight!

115
00:08:38,985 --> 00:08:41,852
Ha! It's the grave-digger's best friend.

116
00:08:41,954 --> 00:08:43,922
The maggot's mate.

117
00:08:43,990 --> 00:08:46,390
Can't you find a civil-tongued
wise woman?

118
00:08:46,459 --> 00:08:49,257
She's the one
the civil-tongued wise women go to.

119
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,761
Hello, baldy.

120
00:08:53,966 --> 00:08:56,400
Do you know who I am? I'm the Sheriff.

121
00:08:57,837 --> 00:08:59,600
And I have a job for you.

122
00:08:59,672 --> 00:09:04,132
If you were on fire, I would not damp you
with my wet underwrappings.

123
00:09:07,079 --> 00:09:09,445
Cure this man or you die,

124
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:14,577
anyone that you love and even some
that you have a passing liking for.

125
00:09:14,654 --> 00:09:18,112
I can't stay here.
My daughter's expecting a baby.

126
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:20,954
Your daughter can expect
a corpse for a mother

127
00:09:21,027 --> 00:09:22,858
if you do not do as you are told.

128
00:09:22,962 --> 00:09:25,931
Well, I won't stay if she lays one finger
on my patient.

129
00:09:32,505 --> 00:09:34,735
If I treat him, can I go?

130
00:09:34,807 --> 00:09:38,038
Do you think I want you
cluttering up my castle?

131
00:09:48,621 --> 00:09:51,351
When he speaks, fetch me immediately.

132
00:09:54,627 --> 00:09:58,063
Well, I'll get rid of
these things for starters.

133
00:10:01,968 --> 00:10:05,597
Sir, there's a sign at the Trip Inn.

134
00:10:05,671 --> 00:10:07,764
Marian!

135
00:10:09,075 --> 00:10:12,738
- Where's your guard?
- I don't know. I must've lost him.

136
00:10:14,046 --> 00:10:16,981
- Watch Lady Marian.
- Is that really necessary?

137
00:10:19,852 --> 00:10:22,446
I don't know. Is it?

138
00:10:22,555 --> 00:10:24,386
Do you think I'm a threat?

139
00:10:25,891 --> 00:10:27,119
No.

140
00:10:27,193 --> 00:10:31,823
I was wondering if I could have a day away
from the castle and the guards

141
00:10:31,897 --> 00:10:34,229
- and accompany you.
- I'm on business.

142
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,791
- Sounds interesting.
- It's private.

143
00:10:36,869 --> 00:10:39,929
- Sounds doubly interesting.
- Marian, no.

144
00:10:40,006 --> 00:10:43,442
Very well but at least let me have a day
unchaperoned.

145
00:10:45,578 --> 00:10:49,412
- You're up to something.
- Yes. I'm charming you,

146
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:53,612
so that I can have an hour or two
without a goon on my back.

147
00:11:01,027 --> 00:11:03,655
But you stay in the castle.

148
00:11:08,634 --> 00:11:09,760
Ah!

149
00:11:23,049 --> 00:11:25,142
Somebody order leeches?

150
00:11:25,217 --> 00:11:28,653
I've seen enough bloodsuckers
for one day, mostly in charge.

151
00:11:28,754 --> 00:11:31,450
Lovely specimens.

152
00:11:31,557 --> 00:11:33,252
Hungry.

153
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,524
Let's take a look.

154
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:45,727
Hmm.

155
00:11:54,413 --> 00:11:56,506
Oh! Robin of Locksley.

156
00:11:56,582 --> 00:12:00,382
What's that beard? Neither grown
nor shaven, make up your mind.

157
00:12:00,453 --> 00:12:02,512
'Ey, Matilda.

158
00:12:02,588 --> 00:12:04,647
- Has this man talked?
- No.

159
00:12:04,757 --> 00:12:07,920
- You can't treat him.
- Good.

160
00:12:07,993 --> 00:12:12,123
Get me out of this dung heap.
My Rosa has a baby on the way.

161
00:12:12,198 --> 00:12:14,666
A boy, I'd wager,
by the trouble he's caused.

162
00:12:14,767 --> 00:12:19,261
Twice turned himself upside down.
You were worse, I seem to remember.

163
00:12:19,371 --> 00:12:22,568
Ha! This'll relax her while I turn him.
Let's go.

164
00:12:22,641 --> 00:12:25,576
- I have business here first.
- She needs me now.

165
00:12:25,644 --> 00:12:29,375
- Do you know anything about this man?
- He was stung by a bee, look.

166
00:12:29,448 --> 00:12:31,973
What, this unwell from a bee sting?

167
00:12:32,051 --> 00:12:34,246
It can happen. Nearly killed him.

168
00:12:34,353 --> 00:12:36,617
That and the leeches.

169
00:12:36,689 --> 00:12:38,657
- But he's all right now.
- Wait.

170
00:12:40,292 --> 00:12:45,423
He's Henry of Lewes. He's come to tell
the Sheriff where the King plans to land.

171
00:12:45,498 --> 00:12:49,161
So, you should turn away.

172
00:12:49,235 --> 00:12:53,137
Stop! Has a dung beetle tunneled
into you and eaten your soul?

173
00:12:53,205 --> 00:12:56,402
- I'll be quick.
- A bee failed to kill him, so did a quack,

174
00:12:56,475 --> 00:13:00,434
I'll be damned if a boy I delivered
sneaks in and kills one of my patients.

175
00:13:00,546 --> 00:13:03,515
Matilda, I can't let him live
to speak his treason.

176
00:13:03,582 --> 00:13:07,177
So it's not his life
you're afraid of, then?

177
00:13:07,253 --> 00:13:09,153
It's his tongue.

178
00:13:11,023 --> 00:13:13,992
So, shall we just cut out his tongue, then?

179
00:13:14,059 --> 00:13:16,118
Oh, men!

180
00:13:16,195 --> 00:13:19,926
Always think in a straight line.
I've got a better idea.

181
00:13:19,999 --> 00:13:23,958
- Can you silence him?
- Long enough to stop you killing him.

182
00:13:24,036 --> 00:13:28,939
I could muddle his brain for a day or two,
confuse and baffle him.

183
00:13:29,008 --> 00:13:30,168
Now...

184
00:13:36,682 --> 00:13:39,048
Oh! Sorry.

185
00:14:01,807 --> 00:14:04,173
- Well?
- Hasn't been in yet.

186
00:14:09,481 --> 00:14:12,177
Must be held up.

187
00:14:12,251 --> 00:14:17,712
When he finally arrives,
give him this for delivering Henry.

188
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:21,624
Tell him it's silver, not gold,
because the goods were damaged.

189
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:23,252
Ahem.

190
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:28,428
Thank you.

191
00:14:33,439 --> 00:14:36,806
He's waking. Matilda, quickly.

192
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:38,707
Where am I?

193
00:14:38,777 --> 00:14:42,406
- What is it?
- Here, it's mead.

194
00:14:44,350 --> 00:14:47,012
There, sir.

195
00:14:47,086 --> 00:14:49,850
Right, job done. Let's go. Come on.

196
00:14:49,955 --> 00:14:53,948
- I have to know that it's worked.
- You want the sun and the stars as well?

197
00:14:54,026 --> 00:14:58,395
He mustn't talk. If we spare his life,
then we sacrifice the King's.

198
00:14:58,464 --> 00:15:01,661
Look lively, you pair of oafs.

199
00:15:05,804 --> 00:15:08,068
Is he awake?

200
00:15:08,173 --> 00:15:09,902
Henry...

201
00:15:09,975 --> 00:15:12,375
Mead - it was horrible.

202
00:15:12,444 --> 00:15:15,106
Henry! My dear Henry!

203
00:15:16,682 --> 00:15:18,707
- Castle.
- Yes. Yes, yes.

204
00:15:18,784 --> 00:15:22,151
- This is Nottingham Castle.
- I've come from the Holy Land.

205
00:15:22,221 --> 00:15:23,916
Yes?

206
00:15:23,989 --> 00:15:27,584
- I'll speak only to the Sheriff.
- Yes, yes. I am the Sheriff,

207
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:29,252
the Sheriff of Nottingham.

208
00:15:29,361 --> 00:15:32,262
- The King...
- Yes? Which port will he arrive at?

209
00:15:32,364 --> 00:15:35,527
- When the King returns from the Holy Land...
- Yes, yes.

210
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:38,161
Where will he land?
What's the King's plan?

211
00:15:38,237 --> 00:15:39,829
- He will land...
- Yes?

212
00:15:40,973 --> 00:15:43,806
L- I feel... I feel strange.

213
00:15:43,876 --> 00:15:45,571
- Yes?
- I feel...

214
00:15:45,644 --> 00:15:48,010
Yes, never mind how you feel,
Henry, hmm?

215
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,139
What's the King's plan?

216
00:15:50,215 --> 00:15:53,446
The plan King's. Planking port.

217
00:15:53,552 --> 00:15:56,521
Yes, yes? Which port?

218
00:15:56,588 --> 00:16:00,354
The pork. I have come from the Holy Pork.

219
00:16:02,761 --> 00:16:05,229
No, no. Which port?

220
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:08,630
Pork. Holy Pork!

221
00:16:13,372 --> 00:16:15,363
- There's someone there!
- Guards!

222
00:16:25,684 --> 00:16:27,242
Give this to Rosa.

223
00:16:27,353 --> 00:16:31,187
- Get out, you rancid faced outlaw!
- Don't stand on him!

224
00:16:31,256 --> 00:16:33,986
Get him up! Get him on the bed.

225
00:16:34,059 --> 00:16:36,721
Gently, gently, gently.

226
00:16:36,795 --> 00:16:39,764
Which port? Which port?

227
00:16:44,803 --> 00:16:46,327
Robin!

228
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:53,140
- Henry?
- He's silenced.

229
00:16:53,212 --> 00:16:54,975
But only temporarily.

230
00:16:55,047 --> 00:16:57,038
You're right - you have a spy.

231
00:16:57,883 --> 00:17:00,977
- How do you know?
- I followed Gisborne to the Trip Inn.

232
00:17:01,053 --> 00:17:04,580
Whoever he was meeting didn't come
but he left money with a maid.

233
00:17:04,656 --> 00:17:07,216
I heard them mention Henry
but no other names.

234
00:17:07,292 --> 00:17:09,590
That's payment for Henry's arrival.

235
00:17:09,661 --> 00:17:12,596
Who is it, Marian? Who would betray me?

236
00:17:15,501 --> 00:17:17,401
There's Gisborne.

237
00:17:26,145 --> 00:17:27,737
Marian...

238
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:31,213
Guy.

239
00:17:31,283 --> 00:17:33,911
- You've been following me.
- Me?

240
00:17:33,986 --> 00:17:35,715
- Don't deny it.
- No, I...

241
00:17:35,788 --> 00:17:38,780
I saw you by the stall, earlier, now here.

242
00:17:38,857 --> 00:17:41,519
- Coincidence? I don't think so.
- But I...

243
00:17:41,593 --> 00:17:43,527
- You disobeyed me.
- Guy, please!

244
00:17:43,595 --> 00:17:48,658
Let me explain. You don't understand.
Punish me but do not punish my father.

245
00:17:48,767 --> 00:17:51,167
Punish you? Why would I punish you?

246
00:17:52,971 --> 00:17:54,370
What have you been doing?

247
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:58,501
Forgive me, you are right. I disobeyed you.

248
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:00,841
I just wanted to spend time with you.

249
00:18:00,946 --> 00:18:03,005
Really?

250
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,811
Yes.

251
00:18:04,883 --> 00:18:06,316
Well...

252
00:18:06,385 --> 00:18:08,512
I'm honored, Marian,

253
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:12,455
but I told you I was on business.

254
00:18:13,992 --> 00:18:16,654
Well, it won't happen again.

255
00:18:18,630 --> 00:18:20,564
Shall we?

256
00:18:37,049 --> 00:18:38,346
What's your problem?

257
00:18:38,417 --> 00:18:40,317
'Ey!

258
00:18:40,385 --> 00:18:43,843
- Did you speak to Robin or what?
- Why do you wanna know?

259
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:46,390
What's going on. What's the plan?

260
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:49,222
Did the messenger get through
to the castle?

261
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:52,786
- Is Robin gonna kill him?
- Like to know his plans, do you?

262
00:18:52,865 --> 00:18:55,925
- What's the Sheriff and Gisborne's plan?
- What?

263
00:18:56,001 --> 00:18:58,629
Is there even a Henry? Or is it a trap?

264
00:18:58,704 --> 00:19:00,968
- What?
- What's going on?

265
00:19:01,039 --> 00:19:03,735
- How much do they pay you?
- Pay who?

266
00:19:05,444 --> 00:19:07,742
There's a spy in the camp.

267
00:19:09,281 --> 00:19:11,545
One of you is a spy.

268
00:19:11,617 --> 00:19:14,415
And Robin knows, so you're done for.

269
00:19:14,486 --> 00:19:17,922
- What? How does he know?
- It's obvious!

270
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:20,550
Gisborne's always
five or six steps ahead.

271
00:19:20,626 --> 00:19:23,117
- Are you calling me a traitor?
- Traitor?

272
00:19:23,195 --> 00:19:25,789
Trai... Oh!

273
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:29,524
What you looking at me for?

274
00:19:29,601 --> 00:19:34,095
You wanted me to steal from Robin,
that time we thought the King was coming?

275
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:37,006
- Right! Traitor!
- We decided against it.

276
00:19:37,075 --> 00:19:39,703
- I said no!
- Stop it, now!

277
00:19:39,778 --> 00:19:43,214
Yes. If anyone's gonna kill the traitor,
it's gonna be me.

278
00:19:43,282 --> 00:19:47,912
What makes you so high and mighty?
If he trusts you, why'd he send you back?

279
00:19:48,487 --> 00:19:50,819
Stop it, the pair of you.

280
00:19:50,889 --> 00:19:53,619
Off him! Stop it.

281
00:19:55,227 --> 00:19:56,421
Robin.

282
00:19:58,363 --> 00:19:59,830
Master!

283
00:20:02,267 --> 00:20:04,394
What is going on?

284
00:20:04,469 --> 00:20:06,903
- We're taking her to the camp.
- Our camp?

285
00:20:06,972 --> 00:20:09,600
- This is Rosa.
- So much for it being a secret.

286
00:20:09,675 --> 00:20:12,644
So much for a lot of things being secrets.

287
00:20:13,645 --> 00:20:15,738
Djaq, the baby's the wrong way round.

288
00:20:15,814 --> 00:20:18,044
Do you know how to turn it?

289
00:20:19,017 --> 00:20:22,453
- Let's get you to a bed, shall we?
- You don't, do you?

290
00:20:31,997 --> 00:20:34,056
Get on with it!

291
00:20:41,139 --> 00:20:43,369
Your Majesty...

292
00:20:43,442 --> 00:20:45,239
He's not the King.

293
00:20:46,278 --> 00:20:49,247
- Mother?
- His brain...

294
00:20:49,314 --> 00:20:51,839
bled to dried pigskin by his leeches.

295
00:20:54,286 --> 00:20:55,810
Er...

296
00:20:57,489 --> 00:20:59,821
Hmm.

297
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:18,503
- She's poisoned him.
- Rubbish!

298
00:21:18,577 --> 00:21:22,104
- I haven't given him anything.
- I hate to tell tales

299
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:29,586
but I've asked around and rumor has it that
she delivered the baby Robin into this world.

300
00:21:33,225 --> 00:21:35,216
Pig. Canker.

301
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:37,819
Blight by name, blight by nature.

302
00:21:39,264 --> 00:21:41,391
"Help. Help.

303
00:21:41,466 --> 00:21:43,331
"There's someone there. "

304
00:21:45,337 --> 00:21:46,998
Oh, nice try.

305
00:21:49,141 --> 00:21:52,770
- You poisoned him, didn't you?
- No!

306
00:21:52,844 --> 00:21:55,711
I just gave him something
to help him sleep.

307
00:21:55,781 --> 00:21:59,512
Well, you can give him something
to wake him up, can't you?

308
00:22:01,420 --> 00:22:03,513
No.

309
00:22:03,588 --> 00:22:06,716
There are wrong answers
and there are right answers.

310
00:22:07,893 --> 00:22:09,451
That was a wrong answer.

311
00:22:12,064 --> 00:22:15,261
We need to know who the traitor is.

312
00:22:15,367 --> 00:22:18,063
I'm sorry. Not the sort of secret I can keep.

313
00:22:20,872 --> 00:22:23,636
- Let's deal with Rosa, first.
- Tell us, Robin.

314
00:22:23,742 --> 00:22:26,540
Robin, there'll be people needing help
every day

315
00:22:26,611 --> 00:22:30,103
- but if you suspect us...
- All right.

316
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:34,243
It's true. One of you is betraying us.

317
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:37,720
You're meeting Gisborne
and you're selling our secrets.

318
00:22:40,292 --> 00:22:42,852
- Not me.
- It's not me, either.

319
00:22:42,961 --> 00:22:44,360
- It's not me.
- Not me.

320
00:22:44,429 --> 00:22:46,260
Stop this, now.

321
00:22:46,365 --> 00:22:50,734
If the guilty man or woman confesses
right here, I'll listen.

322
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:56,974
Tell me what Gisborne said,
what he offered.

323
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:59,101
Step forward now.

324
00:22:59,177 --> 00:23:00,940
You have one chance.

325
00:23:02,647 --> 00:23:05,207
I will not be treated with equal suspicion.

326
00:23:12,791 --> 00:23:16,625
Well, whoever you are,
you've made your choice.

327
00:23:17,863 --> 00:23:19,387
And I will find you out.

328
00:23:22,367 --> 00:23:23,834
Arrgh!

329
00:23:28,006 --> 00:23:30,099
John!

330
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:34,508
- Help me turn the baby.
- No.

331
00:23:35,981 --> 00:23:38,814
I have worked in the battlefields, all men.

332
00:23:38,884 --> 00:23:41,580
- I've never treated this.
- Neither have I.

333
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:56,965
May I?

334
00:24:10,415 --> 00:24:11,939
- Oh!
- What?

335
00:24:12,017 --> 00:24:14,247
It's the head.

336
00:24:14,352 --> 00:24:16,547
Hello, little one.

337
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:19,784
Hello! You're the wrong way round.

338
00:24:19,858 --> 00:24:22,418
You need to turn, baby.

339
00:24:26,498 --> 00:24:27,965
Ahh!

340
00:24:29,501 --> 00:24:32,163
- It moved.
- That's it, that's right.

341
00:24:32,237 --> 00:24:33,795
Yeah?

342
00:24:38,944 --> 00:24:41,811
How did you do that?

343
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:43,745
Oh! Thank you.

344
00:24:44,850 --> 00:24:46,579
Thank you!

345
00:24:52,691 --> 00:24:58,254
My lords, Matilda here somehow managed
to bring a patient of hers

346
00:24:58,363 --> 00:24:59,625
back from the dead.

347
00:24:59,698 --> 00:25:03,031
Certified by my good self - dead!

348
00:25:03,101 --> 00:25:06,559
So what do we have here, hmm?

349
00:25:06,638 --> 00:25:09,573
- Do we have a healer...
- What's happening?

350
00:25:09,641 --> 00:25:14,135
...or something else? A necromancer?
A devil worshipper? No.

351
00:25:14,212 --> 00:25:17,511
- A witch.
- She's not a witch.

352
00:25:17,582 --> 00:25:24,181
So perhaps a ducking in Locksley
pond would calm all our nerves.

353
00:25:24,256 --> 00:25:26,781
Guy, you know she's not a witch.

354
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:30,624
Marian, say nothing. These allegations
spread by association.

355
00:25:30,695 --> 00:25:35,132
- The ducking stool's a death sentence.
- There's nothing you can do for her.

356
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:38,033
Did I leave you to die
when you were being drowned?

357
00:25:39,638 --> 00:25:42,106
Guy! Guy!

358
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:49,241
You could avoid all this, Matilda.
Tell us the antidote.

359
00:26:05,430 --> 00:26:07,762
Boiled Sheriff's brains

360
00:26:07,832 --> 00:26:10,096
with parsley.

361
00:26:16,041 --> 00:26:17,201
To Locksley.

362
00:26:29,988 --> 00:26:32,513
- Djaq.
- Later.

363
00:26:35,627 --> 00:26:37,424
You all right?

364
00:26:37,495 --> 00:26:41,522
There's a spy in the camp.
How can anything be all right?

365
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:44,501
Well, he probably knows
he's made a mistake now.

366
00:26:44,569 --> 00:26:48,369
He had his chance to confess.

367
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:50,965
Maybe he's stuck -
people get stuck, you know.

368
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:58,045
Your brother said he was stuck.
He refused to change and he hanged for it.

369
00:26:58,149 --> 00:27:01,118
- He was an idiot.
- No!

370
00:27:01,186 --> 00:27:05,020
He was a good man underneath it
and you saw that.

371
00:27:07,392 --> 00:27:10,156
And I believe Robin would see it, too.

372
00:27:10,228 --> 00:27:15,564
If the spy confessed
and begged forgiveness...

373
00:27:16,668 --> 00:27:18,727
and changed his ways.

374
00:27:21,673 --> 00:27:24,335
I believe you're a good man, Allan A Dale.

375
00:27:29,247 --> 00:27:32,512
Robin!

376
00:27:33,618 --> 00:27:35,313
Robin!

377
00:27:42,694 --> 00:27:45,060
Robin, Matilda -

378
00:27:45,163 --> 00:27:50,430
the Sheriff knows she helped you,
they're having her dunked as a witch.

379
00:27:50,535 --> 00:27:52,935
- When?
- Now, at Locksley pond.

380
00:27:53,004 --> 00:27:54,972
I have to go before I'm missed.

381
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:57,031
Robin! The baby's coming.

382
00:27:57,976 --> 00:28:00,706
- Baby?
- It's Matilda's grandchild.

383
00:28:00,779 --> 00:28:02,440
Hurry! Hurry!

384
00:28:06,785 --> 00:28:08,844
Matilda needs us.

385
00:28:08,953 --> 00:28:10,978
Djaq, you stay with Rosa.

386
00:28:11,056 --> 00:28:13,718
- Everybody else with me.
- What's happened?

387
00:28:13,792 --> 00:28:15,726
The Sheriff's happened.

388
00:28:15,794 --> 00:28:18,729
John - can you stay?

389
00:28:34,946 --> 00:28:37,915
Has he said anything sensible yet?

390
00:28:44,155 --> 00:28:45,747
Lords, ladies,

391
00:28:45,824 --> 00:28:48,258
- peasants...
- Presents.

392
00:28:48,359 --> 00:28:52,557
- Pheasants.
- Have a look at this noble man.

393
00:28:52,630 --> 00:28:55,497
He returned from the dead, possessed.

394
00:28:56,668 --> 00:28:58,602
The witch shall be ducked.

395
00:29:00,004 --> 00:29:04,907
If she dies, it proves the devil
has abandoned her

396
00:29:04,976 --> 00:29:07,570
and she shall be buried
on consecrated ground.

397
00:29:07,645 --> 00:29:10,011
Constipated ground.

398
00:29:11,483 --> 00:29:15,613
If she lives, showing the devil
still to be in her,

399
00:29:15,687 --> 00:29:18,349
she shall be burnt alive.

400
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:20,823
Hard to know which one to hope for.

401
00:29:20,892 --> 00:29:23,986
Rosa! My Rosa!

402
00:29:24,062 --> 00:29:26,121
Ah! Down she goes.

403
00:29:27,799 --> 00:29:30,290
Deep breath.

404
00:29:42,547 --> 00:29:44,708
Oh, lovely grapes, Gisborne.

405
00:30:07,005 --> 00:30:11,169
You weasel-faced whore-son.

406
00:30:11,242 --> 00:30:14,040
Sorry? Who? Robin? Robin's not here.

407
00:30:16,381 --> 00:30:20,010
And three, two, one.

408
00:30:22,086 --> 00:30:24,111
Deep breath, deep breath.

409
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:34,321
There's something...

410
00:30:37,368 --> 00:30:40,098
- Oh, what's happening?
- It's fine.

411
00:30:40,171 --> 00:30:42,696
Your husband, is he away?

412
00:30:44,042 --> 00:30:46,567
- The wars.
- He'll be so proud.

413
00:30:49,280 --> 00:30:51,771
- What's your wife's name?
- Alice.

414
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:54,182
So you've done this before?

415
00:30:55,186 --> 00:31:00,419
- With Alice? Why is it so hard?
- No, I was an outlaw,

416
00:31:00,491 --> 00:31:03,790
in the forest, Alice was alone.

417
00:31:08,666 --> 00:31:11,294
Push now!

418
00:31:16,975 --> 00:31:19,136
# Ba-ba ba-boom #

419
00:32:01,085 --> 00:32:02,985
I curse you.

420
00:32:03,054 --> 00:32:07,753
May snakes crawl up your nose holes

421
00:32:07,825 --> 00:32:11,659
and feed on your tiny brain.

422
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:14,231
Down! Down, down.

423
00:32:34,085 --> 00:32:35,712
Breathe, slowly.

424
00:32:43,194 --> 00:32:45,958
It's difficult to take him - Henry.

425
00:32:46,030 --> 00:32:47,827
Can't we just kill him?

426
00:32:47,932 --> 00:32:50,799
Draw attention to Robin, won't it?
Put him in danger.

427
00:32:50,868 --> 00:32:54,326
We bide our time
and wait till they're distracted.

428
00:32:54,405 --> 00:32:56,600
Unless one of you's informed Gisborne.

429
00:32:56,674 --> 00:33:00,542
- Oi! Keep your accusations to yourself.
- You keep pumping.

430
00:33:01,579 --> 00:33:05,242
Let's lift up the carcass. Ha ha ha!

431
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:09,112
Ten, nine, eight...

432
00:33:09,187 --> 00:33:12,247
...Seven, six,

433
00:33:12,357 --> 00:33:15,155
five, four...

434
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:18,428
three, two...

435
00:33:18,496 --> 00:33:20,123
And a half.

436
00:33:20,198 --> 00:33:22,393
One and a half.

437
00:33:22,467 --> 00:33:24,526
And bring her up.

438
00:33:41,285 --> 00:33:43,753
What the devil is that, Blight?

439
00:33:43,821 --> 00:33:47,917
I... I suspect they may be
her underwrappings, my lord.

440
00:33:47,992 --> 00:33:50,790
Shut up! Shut up!

441
00:33:53,398 --> 00:33:55,389
Arrest, arrest...

442
00:33:55,466 --> 00:33:57,297
Gisborne! Henry's gone!

443
00:33:57,368 --> 00:33:59,427
- Henry's gone!
- Guards!

444
00:33:59,537 --> 00:34:01,232
Find him!

445
00:34:14,852 --> 00:34:17,013
Rosa! Where's my Rosa?

446
00:34:18,189 --> 00:34:20,953
Oh! Rosa!

447
00:34:22,760 --> 00:34:25,354
- Mother?
- Where's the little lad?

448
00:34:25,430 --> 00:34:28,593
- Tell me the lad's all right?
- No lad.

449
00:34:28,666 --> 00:34:31,157
No lad?

450
00:34:35,039 --> 00:34:37,701
She's a girl.

451
00:34:39,410 --> 00:34:41,435
Good lungs, she has.

452
00:34:41,546 --> 00:34:43,207
Not a moment's peace.

453
00:34:43,281 --> 00:34:47,547
Well, let's see if a damp grandmother
can't set her off again.

454
00:34:47,618 --> 00:34:51,520
Oh! Oh, there, my little...

455
00:34:53,624 --> 00:34:55,990
- What's her name?
- Alice.

456
00:34:56,060 --> 00:34:58,426
I'm going to call her Alice.

457
00:34:58,496 --> 00:34:59,929
Alice.

458
00:35:09,607 --> 00:35:11,802
Still in the land of fairies.

459
00:35:12,477 --> 00:35:14,707
What are you gonna do with him?

460
00:35:15,947 --> 00:35:18,347
- I'll banish him.
- We should kill him.

461
00:35:18,416 --> 00:35:22,978
- A traitor doesn't deserve to live.
- Kill him?

462
00:35:23,054 --> 00:35:25,113
Congratulations, Grandma.

463
00:35:26,824 --> 00:35:29,384
Oi, Much! Look!

464
00:35:30,094 --> 00:35:31,994
Much, meet Alice.

465
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:45,300
- Put it down, Henry.
- Thought you don't kill any more?

466
00:35:45,376 --> 00:35:49,142
- For the King, I kill.
- The King's finished.

467
00:35:49,213 --> 00:35:52,239
The Sheriff, Prince John,
the Black Knights, all win.

468
00:35:52,350 --> 00:35:54,648
Robin!

469
00:36:08,666 --> 00:36:10,896
Not today they won't.

470
00:36:20,244 --> 00:36:23,771
- Can I trust you, Will?
- Of course.

471
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:28,982
- I need your help.
- Anything.

472
00:36:29,053 --> 00:36:33,615
Marian saw a maid speaking to Gisborne
at the Trip - she'll know who our spy is.

473
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:38,128
I can go to the Trip and make the maid
tell me who the traitor is.

474
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:41,131
- You go back to the camp at sundown.
- Where am I going?

475
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:44,630
This is gonna hurt.

476
00:36:48,806 --> 00:36:50,137
What's he doing?

477
00:36:51,642 --> 00:36:54,736
- Robin!
- Master!

478
00:36:54,812 --> 00:36:56,746
Sundown, remember?

479
00:37:03,588 --> 00:37:05,988
I knew it was him! I knew it was him!

480
00:37:06,057 --> 00:37:09,515
- But Will?
- No.

481
00:37:09,594 --> 00:37:12,119
- I knew it.
- Robin...

482
00:37:12,196 --> 00:37:15,290
Will's the spy. The subject's closed.

483
00:37:15,366 --> 00:37:18,028
Will? Robin, I do not believe.

484
00:37:18,135 --> 00:37:20,831
- I need to speak with you.
- Not now.

485
00:37:20,938 --> 00:37:24,738
- Believe me, Robin...
- No, you don't, Djaq. Trust me.

486
00:37:25,876 --> 00:37:28,367
Will's gone and that's the end of it.

487
00:37:28,446 --> 00:37:30,914
I'm have to go to the castle.
He had a go-between.

488
00:37:30,982 --> 00:37:32,916
- At the castle?
- At the Trip.

489
00:37:32,984 --> 00:37:36,351
Marian saw a serving girl
receiving money from Gisborne.

490
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:39,719
I have to meet Marian
to find out what Gisborne knows.

491
00:37:39,790 --> 00:37:42,918
- We'll come.
- No, no. I'm safer on my own.

492
00:37:42,994 --> 00:37:47,226
Meanwhile, you lot have to scatter
in case Gisborne knows about the camp.

493
00:37:47,331 --> 00:37:49,356
I'll go to the Trip at sundown.

494
00:37:49,433 --> 00:37:51,560
Come back here after that.

495
00:37:51,636 --> 00:37:53,900
I'll tell you what I know.

496
00:37:56,941 --> 00:37:58,704
What are we gonna do?

497
00:37:58,776 --> 00:38:01,040
You heard him - we scatter.

498
00:38:05,983 --> 00:38:09,646
You're late. I was going to keep
your money back.

499
00:38:12,356 --> 00:38:14,347
Silver.

500
00:38:14,425 --> 00:38:15,983
Not gold.

501
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:21,225
You were gonna tell Gisborne to keep it.
I'm not doing this any more, all right?

502
00:38:21,332 --> 00:38:24,927
- It's a bit late for a conscience, isn't it?
- Yeah, very late.

503
00:38:30,608 --> 00:38:32,337
Robin.

504
00:38:43,988 --> 00:38:45,546
You're early.

505
00:38:45,623 --> 00:38:47,557
- Leave us.
- Stay there.

506
00:38:47,625 --> 00:38:49,252
Get out.

507
00:38:55,666 --> 00:38:59,329
I need to talk to my spy.

508
00:39:03,274 --> 00:39:06,243
What was that with Will?
You banished Will.

509
00:39:06,344 --> 00:39:08,710
It was an act.

510
00:39:08,779 --> 00:39:11,304
Only she knew who was guilty.

511
00:39:11,382 --> 00:39:15,341
And I knew the spy would want to come
here before me to cover his tracks.

512
00:39:15,419 --> 00:39:18,547
For all I knew, it could've been Will
standing there.

513
00:39:19,623 --> 00:39:21,716
But it's not, is it?

514
00:39:24,762 --> 00:39:26,423
It's you.

515
00:39:26,530 --> 00:39:28,896
Robin, it was over.

516
00:39:28,966 --> 00:39:31,230
Ask her. I made a decision.

517
00:39:31,335 --> 00:39:34,099
- Then what's this?
- I was giving it back.

518
00:39:36,474 --> 00:39:40,911
So you'd betray me,
you'd betray yourself, betray your King,

519
00:39:40,978 --> 00:39:42,741
for what?

520
00:39:42,813 --> 00:39:45,748
For a few silver coins.

521
00:39:45,816 --> 00:39:48,216
What have you told Gisborne, Allan?

522
00:39:49,420 --> 00:39:50,910
- Huh?
- I...

523
00:39:50,988 --> 00:39:53,252
Nothing, really.

524
00:39:54,458 --> 00:39:57,518
- Does he know about the camp?
- No!

525
00:39:57,595 --> 00:40:00,928
- Does he know about Marian?
- No.

526
00:40:03,467 --> 00:40:05,298
- More lies?
- No!

527
00:40:07,605 --> 00:40:09,573
This was the last time, I promise.

528
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:12,165
And I was wrong.

529
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:14,711
He captured me, tortured me -
I had no choice.

530
00:40:14,779 --> 00:40:17,407
Everything is a choice!

531
00:40:17,481 --> 00:40:19,915
Everything we do.

532
00:40:23,788 --> 00:40:26,416
That's easy for you to say, though, isn't it?

533
00:40:27,358 --> 00:40:28,985
Yeah?

534
00:40:29,059 --> 00:40:33,587
You get the glory, you get the girl,
everyone loves you.

535
00:40:33,664 --> 00:40:37,930
Then when the King comes back,
you'll have property, a wife - everything.

536
00:40:38,002 --> 00:40:40,698
What will I have?

537
00:40:42,973 --> 00:40:46,909
You are always in the sun, Robin,
and I'm always in the shade.

538
00:40:47,945 --> 00:40:50,607
Is that meant to be an excuse? Huh?

539
00:40:52,016 --> 00:40:54,211
Give me another chance, please.

540
00:40:55,286 --> 00:40:58,847
I wouldn't have let Gisborne hurt any of us.

541
00:40:58,956 --> 00:41:03,393
Harmless lies, innocent betrayals -
they don't exist, Allan.

542
00:41:04,662 --> 00:41:07,153
Robin, I've changed.

543
00:41:07,231 --> 00:41:09,529
How can I get you to believe that?

544
00:41:10,568 --> 00:41:12,502
You can't.

545
00:41:12,570 --> 00:41:14,765
And the funny thing is...

546
00:41:16,273 --> 00:41:19,140
- you might be telling the truth.
- I am!

547
00:41:19,210 --> 00:41:21,542
How am I supposed to believe you
any more?

548
00:41:21,612 --> 00:41:25,639
Robin... I swear to you on my life...

549
00:41:30,788 --> 00:41:32,415
Don't kill me.

550
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:34,651
Please.

551
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:46,902
You're lucky I've left you with a life
to swear upon.

552
00:41:47,838 --> 00:41:50,568
Never, never...

553
00:41:50,641 --> 00:41:53,439
let me set eyes on you again.

554
00:42:07,157 --> 00:42:09,125
Are we safe?

555
00:42:11,862 --> 00:42:13,227
Will!

556
00:42:14,798 --> 00:42:17,130
- Will!
- It's all right.

557
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:19,601
It's all right. It wasn't him.

558
00:42:20,404 --> 00:42:22,702
What?

559
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:26,169
It was a trap.

560
00:42:26,243 --> 00:42:28,370
I lied to you, I'm sorry.

561
00:42:28,445 --> 00:42:30,140
I had to lure the spy.

562
00:42:35,152 --> 00:42:37,950
- It was Allan.
- Is he alive?

563
00:42:39,623 --> 00:42:41,318
- Where?
- He's gone.

564
00:42:41,392 --> 00:42:43,257
Allan? Why?

565
00:42:43,327 --> 00:42:45,454
For money, John, why else?

566
00:42:45,529 --> 00:42:47,929
I believe he could've changed.

567
00:42:48,966 --> 00:42:51,901
- You knew it was him?
- I didn't know, I guessed.

568
00:42:52,770 --> 00:42:55,295
I knew it was him. I knew it was Allan.

569
00:42:56,974 --> 00:42:59,636
Will, do you forgive me?

570
00:43:01,378 --> 00:43:03,107
It worked.

571
00:43:03,180 --> 00:43:06,513
And the rest of you?

572
00:43:08,385 --> 00:43:10,376
Travelers on the north road.

573
00:43:11,755 --> 00:43:15,521
Right. Are you with me?

574
00:43:16,727 --> 00:43:18,354
Yeah?

575
00:43:18,429 --> 00:43:20,226
Well, then, let's go.

